From e267be11ce95b05d113f74684855ac5664d7dbeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:48:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: About shows the eMMC

AD5X boards come with different eMMC parts (58A398, A31M8C, MMC8GB so
far), and which one a printer has matters for support. Settings -> About
now names it:

  eMMC       A31M8C (maker 0xEC), PRV 0x30, 58.2 GiB

The row comes from /sys/block/mmcblk0 (name, manfid, prv and size), so it
works on every kernel. It is hidden when mmcblk0 is not an eMMC.

Kiln builds only (HELIX_KILN_AD5X); elsewhere the row stays hidden.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
